          html: `<p>Amazon DynamoDB (launched in 2012) shares a name and some history with Dynamo but not its replication model: its 2022 paper describes a Multi-Paxos-elected leader per partition, with replicas spread across availability zones. Amazon Aurora uses quorums too, but underneath a single-writer database: its storage layer keeps six copies of the data across three availability zones and treats a write as durable once four of the six have it. Cassandra has evolved as well; version 4.0 removed the probabilistic background read repair options (<code>read_repair_chance</code> and <code>dclocal_read_repair_chance</code>).</p>`,
